  "question": {
    "text": "Five numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are randomly selected from the numbers<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn></math> &nbsp;and are arranged in the increasing order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>. The probability that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math>&nbsp;is"
  },
